% ============================================================================
% dolch-sight-word-level.query.adj — worked recall over the
% dolch-sight-word-level library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "which Dolch reading
% level is this sight word taught at?" (direct) or "which words are taught
% at this Dolch level?" (reverse, many-answer) — it states no fact of its
% own — it only `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries.
% ============================================================================

import "dolch-sight-word-level.adj"

? dolch_sight_word_level(the, $Level)          % expect pre_primer (direct)
? dolch_sight_word_level(funny, $Level)        % expect pre_primer (direct, the 40th/last Pre-Primer word -- confirms the completed level)
? dolch_sight_word_level($W, pre_primer)       % expect all 40 Pre-Primer words (reverse, many-answer -- the completed level)
? dolch_sight_word_level(would, $Level)        % expect second_grade (direct, a different level)
? dolch_sight_word_level(they, $Level)         % expect abstain -- a REAL Dolch Primer word, but Primer still ships only its first-five subset
? dolch_sight_word_level(elephant, $Level)     % expect abstain -- not a Dolch word at all
